NEARS-1559 QA - method note (why the offline ACs were driven by cutting the API, not by airplane mode)

First attempt: adb shell cmd connectivity airplane-mode enable + svc wifi/data disable, then
pull-to-refresh on Home. Result: the app left Home entirely and rendered its global
"No internet connection / Oops! / Try Again" screen (see
note-airplane-mode-shows-global-no-internet-screen.png). That screen is driven by the splash-level
connectivity_plus listener (UserApp/lib/features/splash/screens/splash_screen.dart), which
pre-empts Home before the header's own offline arms can be exercised.

So an OS-level network kill cannot reach HomeAppBar's warm-cache / no-cache arms at all.
The offline ACs were instead driven by keeping the network interface UP and making the API
unreachable, which is what actually produces a failed fetch on a live Home:

  build:  flutter run --dart-define=API_HOST=localhost:8000
  online: adb reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000
  offline: adb reverse --remove tcp:8000     (device: "nc 127.0.0.1 8000" -> Connection refused)

The shared dev backend on port 8000 was never stopped - other sessions were unaffected.
